<mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" value="Doing a COLUMN (vertical) op on a row-major image: stock RVV (two ways)  vs  T1 vertical mode" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#212121;"><mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="1320" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note" parent="1" vertex="1" value="Row colour = one cache line. On a 1-D machine the image lives in MEMORY, so changing orientation round-trips through cache/DRAM. On T1 it stays in the register file." style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=10;fontColor=#5D6D7E;"><mxGeometry x="0" y="26" width="1320" height="16" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
